            "result_text": "Perfect! I've created `/app/filter.py` with full XSS attack prevention. Here's what it does:\n\n**Features:**\n- **Removes `<script>` tags** - Eliminates inline and external script blocks\n- **Removes event handlers** - Strips attributes like `onclick`, `onerror`, `onload`, `onchange`, `ondblclick`, `onmouseover`, `onsubmit`, etc. (26+ event types)\n- **Removes `javascript:` protocol** - Handles case-insensitive removal (e.g., `JAVASCRIPT:`, `javascript:`)\n- **Preserves HTML structure** - All legitimate tags, attributes, formatting, and content remain intact\n- **In-place modification** - Modifies the file specified in argv[1]\n\n**Tested scenarios:**\n- ✓ Multiple script tags\n- ✓ Single and double-quoted event handlers\n- ✓ Mixed-case JavaScript protocol\n- ✓ Whitespace variations around attribute equals signs\n- ✓ Script content containing `>` and `<` characters\n- ✓ Real-world HTML with tables, lists, semantic elements, valid links\n\nThe script preserves all non-dangerous attributes (`class`, `id`, `href`, `src`, `type`, `data-*`, etc.) and maintains the exact HTML formatting."
